===Etymology===
{{ja-kanjitab|みそぎ|yomi=k|alt=禊ぎ}}
[[File:Misogi_Harai_Waterfall.JPG|thumb|250px|{{m|ja||禊|tr=misogi}}: a man performing '''''[[misogi]]''''' at [[night]] under a [[waterfall]] at {{w|Tsubaki Grand Shrine}}.]]
{{wp|ja:}}
{{wp|Misogi}}

From {{inh|ja|ojp|sort=みそぎ|-}}, though the original pronunciation of the initial ''miso'' is likely unknown.

The term itself is derived from the {{m|ja|連用形|tr=ren'yōkei||stem or continuative form}} of verb {{m|ja|禊ぐ|tr=misogu||to [[perform]] [[ablution]]s (on someone)|pos=archaic}}.<ref name="KDJ">{{R:Kokugo Dai Jiten}}</ref>

Some sources<ref name="KDJ">{{R:Kokugo Dai Jiten}}</ref><ref name="JDB">{{R:JDB}}</ref> suggest that this might be derived further from a compound of {{m|ja|身|tr=mi||[[body]]}} + {{m|ja|注ぐ|注ぎ|tr=sosogi|[[pour]]ing over, into, onto}}, or alternatively from {{m|ja|水|tr=mi||[[water]]}} + {{m|ja||注ぎ|tr=sosogi|pouring over, into, onto}}.  Considering that {{m|ja||身}} had an ancient reading of {{IPAfont|⟨mi<sub>2</sub>⟩}}, while {{m|ja||水}} had an ancient reading of {{IPAfont|⟨mi<sub>1</sub>⟩}}, the latter is a better potential match.

