===Glyph origin===
{{Han etym}}
Unclear. ''{{w|Shuowen}}'' considers it to be an {{Han compound|甶|禸|ls=ic|t1=head of a ghost|t2=to trample|nocap=y}} – a kind of monkey.

In the bronze script, the top of the character resembles the head of a ghost ({{zh-l|*鬼}}) and/or a mask ([[異]]) and the bottom resembles {{zh-l|*禹}}. {{zh-ref|Zhang et al. (1996)}} considers this character differentiated ({{zh-l|*分化}}) from {{zh-l|*禹}} and that the character is a {{liushu|p|nocap=y}} of a kind of insect with a decorative mark, similar to the one in {{zh-l|*萬|scorpion}}.

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|zh|sit-pro|*ŋaːw||monkey}}; compare {{cog|tbq-kuk-pro|*ŋaaw||long-tailed / grey monkey}}, whence {{cog|lus|ngao||grey monkey}} ({{zh-ref|Schuessler, 2007}}; {{zh-ref|Sagart and Baxter, 2016}}).

