===Etymology===
Attested relatively late, in the Tang dynasty ({{zh-ref|Sagart, 2011}}).

{{zh-ref|Haudricourt and Strecker (1991)}} propose a {{der|zh|hmx}} origin, but {{zh-ref|Sagart (2011)}} argues that the direction of borrowing should be the other way around. He instead proposes an internal Chinese origin, suggesting that it is a cognate of {{och-l|英|grasses at their growing/flowering stage, before producing seeds}} without a ''-r-'' infix.

Relationship with {{cog|tbq}} items is unclear, due to mismatching initials: {{cog|bo|ལྗང་བ||shoot, sprout}}, {{m|bo|ལྗང་བུ||rice seedling}}, {{cog|lep|ᰊᰜᰤᰨᰵ|tr=ta-lyong|t=young blades of corn, rice}} ({{zh-ref|Schuessler, 2007}}).

